Handbook §26. Without this file the host applies its own processing to what is
published, and that processing SILENTLY DROPS files and directories whose names begin with an
underscore or a dot — including _headers and _redirects, which are exactly the files that carry the
controls this class of site has nowhere else to put.

Nothing notices. The site renders, the missing headers produce no error, and the absent control
looks exactly like a site that never needed one.

Keep this file. If the host does not need it, it costs one inode.
